note How this repository moves to a new omega-mv build, read by pin-follow.sh when omega-mv lands a new
note seed/out/omc. Scope: PIN is the compiler pin of backend/amd/kfd/launch only. backend/amd/kfd/launch/COMPILER
note is generated from PIN by `make pin-compiler` (the format is written once, in the Makefile); `make
note test-pin-sync` (in make test) regenerates it and fails when the committed file differs.
note Not yet driven by PIN: every file that still types its own compiler pin. `make pin-hand-list` prints them
note (generated from the omega-mv store each time; no list is kept here).
note A PIN that is current therefore says nothing about those; moving them needs their gates rerun at the new omc.
regen make pin-compiler
gate pin-sync make test-pin-sync
gate amd-launch make test-amd-launch AMD_LAUNCH_OMC="$OMC"
